Revision history for tCMS

0.01 2026-11-06 TEODESIAN
    - Build with Dist::Zilla.  dist.ini, prereqs.yml and metamerge.yml replace
      Makefile.PL, and metamerge.yml names the system packages that tCMS needs.
    - The history before this is in CHANGELOG.
    - Transcode an uploaded video in a Minion queue (data/jobs.db). The worker
      of bin/tcms-jobs runs the jobs. A post lists an AV1 file and an H.264
      file, each with its index first, and serves the original until they
      exist.
    - Show the jobs to admins at /admin/jobs.
    - Add bin/tcms-transcode-existing, which queues the videos that are
      already uploaded.
    - Declare ffmpeg as a system package that tCMS needs.
    - Show on /config the commit that tCMS, tPSGI and a theme that is a git
      checkout run, and whether the upstream has a newer one.  An admin can
      fast forward a checkout that is behind, in the job queue.  The update
      refuses when the new commits need a system package or a perl module.
    - Declare git as a system package that tCMS needs.
    - Give each failed job on /admin/jobs a button that puts it back in the
      queue.  A transcode that runs again skips the outputs that it made.
